												<span class="elementor-toggle-icon elementor-toggle-icon-left" aria-hidden="true">
															<span class="elementor-toggle-icon-closed"><svg class="e-font-icon-svg e-fas-caret-right" viewBox="0 0 192 512" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><path d="M0 384.662V127.338c0-17.818 21.543-26.741 34.142-14.142l128.662 128.662c7.81 7.81 7.81 20.474 0 28.284L34.142 398.804C21.543 411.404 0 402.48 0 384.662z"></path></svg></span>
								<span class="elementor-toggle-icon-opened"><svg class="elementor-toggle-icon-opened e-font-icon-svg e-fas-caret-up" viewBox="0 0 320 512" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><path d="M288.662 352H31.338c-17.818 0-26.741-21.543-14.142-34.142l128.662-128.662c7.81-7.81 20.474-7.81 28.284 0l128.662 128.662c12.6 12.599 3.676 34.142-14.142 34.142z"></path></svg></span>
													</span>
												<a class="elementor-toggle-title" tabindex="0">Which regulations require documented cloud exit strategies?</a>
					</div>

					<div id="elementor-tab-content-1955" class="elementor-tab-content elementor-clearfix" data-tab="5" role="region" aria-labelledby="elementor-tab-title-1955"><p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Frameworks including DORA, FFIEC guidance, HIPAA, and ISO 22301 require or expect documented cloud exit strategies for critical systems, and these are commonly reviewed during audits and vendor risk assessments.</span></p></div>
				</div>
							<div class="elementor-toggle-item">
					<div id="elementor-tab-title-1956" class="elementor-tab-title" data-tab="6" role="button" aria-controls="elementor-tab-content-1956" aria-expanded="false">
												<span class="elementor-toggle-icon elementor-toggle-icon-left" aria-hidden="true">
															<span class="elementor-toggle-icon-closed"><svg class="e-font-icon-svg e-fas-caret-right" viewBox="0 0 192 512" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><path d="M0 384.662V127.338c0-17.818 21.543-26.741 34.142-14.142l128.662 128.662c7.81 7.81 7.81 20.474 0 28.284L34.142 398.804C21.543 411.404 0 402.48 0 384.662z"></path></svg></span>
								<span class="elementor-toggle-icon-opened"><svg class="elementor-toggle-icon-opened e-font-icon-svg e-fas-caret-up" viewBox="0 0 320 512" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><path d="M288.662 352H31.338c-17.818 0-26.741-21.543-14.142-34.142l128.662-128.662c7.81-7.81 20.474-7.81 28.284 0l128.662 128.662c12.6 12.599 3.676 34.142-14.142 34.142z"></path></svg></span>
													</span>
												<a class="elementor-toggle-title" tabindex="0">How often should a cloud exit strategy be tested?</a>
					</div>

					<div id="elementor-tab-content-1956" class="elementor-tab-content elementor-clearfix" data-tab="6" role="region" aria-labelledby="elementor-tab-title-1956"><p><span style="font-weight: 400;"> A cloud exit strategy should be tested at least annually through tabletop exercises, since untested assumptions about data extraction and recovery timelines tend to break down under real conditions.</span></p></div>
				</div>
								</div>
						</div>
				<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-3eb5784 elementor-widget elementor-widget-heading" data-id="3eb5784" data-element_type="widget" data-e-type="widget" data-widget_type="heading.default">
					<h2 class="elementor-heading-title elementor-size-default">Glossary of Terms</h2>				</div>
				<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-964ad45 elementor-widget elementor-widget-toggle" data-id="964ad45" data-element_type="widget" data-e-type="widget" data-widget_type="toggle.default">
							<div class="elementor-toggle">
							<div class="elementor-toggle-item">
					<div id="elementor-tab-title-1571" class="elementor-tab-title" data-tab="1" role="button" aria-controls="elementor-tab-content-1571" aria-expanded="false">
												<span class="elementor-toggle-icon elementor-toggle-icon-left" aria-hidden="true">
															<span class="elementor-toggle-icon-closed"><svg class="e-font-icon-svg e-fas-caret-right" viewBox="0 0 192 512" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><path d="M0 384.662V127.338c0-17.818 21.543-26.741 34.142-14.142l128.662 128.662c7.81 7.81 7.81 20.474 0 28.284L34.142 398.804C21.543 411.404 0 402.48 0 384.662z"></path></svg></span>
								<span class="elementor-toggle-icon-opened"><svg class="elementor-toggle-icon-opened e-font-icon-svg e-fas-caret-up" viewBox="0 0 320 512" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><path d="M288.662 352H31.338c-17.818 0-26.741-21.543-14.142-34.142l128.662-128.662c7.81-7.81 20.474-7.81 28.284 0l128.662 128.662c12.6 12.599 3.676 34.142-14.142 34.142z"></path></svg></span>
													</span>
												<a class="elementor-toggle-title" tabindex="0">Cloud Exit Strateg</a>
					</div>

					<div id="elementor-tab-content-1571" class="elementor-tab-content elementor-clearfix" data-tab="1" role="region" aria-labelledby="elementor-tab-title-1571"><p><span style="font-weight: 400;">A documented plan for transitioning away from a cloud or SaaS provider without disrupting business operations.</span></p></div>
				</div>
							<div class="elementor-toggle-item">
					<div id="elementor-tab-title-1572" class="elementor-tab-title" data-tab="2" role="button" aria-controls="elementor-tab-content-1572" aria-expanded="false">
												<span class="elementor-toggle-icon elementor-toggle-icon-left" aria-hidden="true">
															<span class="elementor-toggle-icon-closed"><svg class="e-font-icon-svg e-fas-caret-right" viewBox="0 0 192 512" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><path d="M0 384.662V127.338c0-17.818 21.543-26.741 34.142-14.142l128.662 128.662c7.81 7.81 7.81 20.474 0 28.284L34.142 398.804C21.543 411.404 0 402.48 0 384.662z"></path></svg></span>
								<span class="elementor-toggle-icon-opened"><svg class="elementor-toggle-icon-opened e-font-icon-svg e-fas-caret-up" viewBox="0 0 320 512" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><path d="M288.662 352H31.338c-17.818 0-26.741-21.543-14.142-34.142l128.662-128.662c7.81-7.81 20.474-7.81 28.284 0l128.662 128.662c12.6 12.599 3.676 34.142-14.142 34.142z"></path></svg></span>
													</span>
												<a class="elementor-toggle-title" tabindex="0">Cloud Vendor Lock-In</a>
					</div>

					<div id="elementor-tab-content-1572" class="elementor-tab-content elementor-clearfix" data-tab="2" role="region" aria-labelledby="elementor-tab-title-1572"><p><span style="font-weight: 400;">A condition where switching cloud providers becomes too costly, complex, or operationally disruptive to execute.</span></p></div>
				</div>
							<div class="elementor-toggle-item">
					<div id="elementor-tab-title-1573" class="elementor-tab-title" data-tab="3" role="button" aria-controls="elementor-tab-content-1573" aria-expanded="false">
												<span class="elementor-toggle-icon elementor-toggle-icon-left" aria-hidden="true">
															<span class="elementor-toggle-icon-closed"><svg class="e-font-icon-svg e-fas-caret-right" viewBox="0 0 192 512" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><path d="M0 384.662V127.338c0-17.818 21.543-26.741 34.142-14.142l128.662 128.662c7.81 7.81 7.81 20.474 0 28.284L34.142 398.804C21.543 411.404 0 402.48 0 384.662z"></path></svg></span>
								<span class="elementor-toggle-icon-opened"><svg class="elementor-toggle-icon-opened e-font-icon-svg e-fas-caret-up" viewBox="0 0 320 512" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><path d="M288.662 352H31.338c-17.818 0-26.741-21.543-14.142-34.142l128.662-128.662c7.81-7.81 20.474-7.81 28.284 0l128.662 128.662c12.6 12.599 3.676 34.142-14.142 34.142z"></path></svg></span>
													</span>
												<a class="elementor-toggle-title" tabindex="0">Cloud Escrow</a>
					</div>

					<div id="elementor-tab-content-1573" class="elementor-tab-content elementor-clearfix" data-tab="3" role="region" aria-labelledby="elementor-tab-title-1573"><p><span style="font-weight: 400;">An escrow arrangement covering the source code, infrastructure configuration, and deployment assets needed to rebuild and operate a cloud-based application.</span></p></div>
				</div>
							<div class="elementor-toggle-item">
					<div id="elementor-tab-title-1574" class="elementor-tab-title" data-tab="4" role="button" aria-controls="elementor-tab-content-1574" aria-expanded="false">
												<span class="elementor-toggle-icon elementor-toggle-icon-left" aria-hidden="true">
															<span class="elementor-toggle-icon-closed"><svg class="e-font-icon-svg e-fas-caret-right" viewBox="0 0 192 512" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><path d="M0 384.662V127.338c0-17.818 21.543-26.741 34.142-14.142l128.662 128.662c7.81 7.81 7.81 20.474 0 28.284L34.142 398.804C21.543 411.404 0 402.48 0 384.662z"></path></svg></span>
								<span class="elementor-toggle-icon-opened"><svg class="elementor-toggle-icon-opened e-font-icon-svg e-fas-caret-up" viewBox="0 0 320 512" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><path d="M288.662 352H31.338c-17.818 0-26.741-21.543-14.142-34.142l128.662-128.662c7.81-7.81 20.474-7.81 28.284 0l128.662 128.662c12.6 12.599 3.676 34.142-14.142 34.142z"></path></svg></span>
													</span>
												<a class="elementor-toggle-title" tabindex="0">Data Portability</a>
					</div>

					<div id="elementor-tab-content-1574" class="elementor-tab-content elementor-clearfix" data-tab="4" role="region" aria-labelledby="elementor-tab-title-1574"><p><span style="font-weight: 400;">The ability to export an organization&#8217;s data in a structured, machine-readable format for use outside the originating platform.</span></p></div>
				</div>
							<div class="elementor-toggle-item">
					<div id="elementor-tab-title-1575" class="elementor-tab-title" data-tab="5" role="button" aria-controls="elementor-tab-content-1575" aria-expanded="false">
												<span class="elementor-toggle-icon elementor-toggle-icon-left" aria-hidden="true">
															<span class="elementor-toggle-icon-closed"><svg class="e-font-icon-svg e-fas-caret-right" viewBox="0 0 192 512" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><path d="M0 384.662V127.338c0-17.818 21.543-26.741 34.142-14.142l128.662 128.662c7.81 7.81 7.81 20.474 0 28.284L34.142 398.804C21.543 411.404 0 402.48 0 384.662z"></path></svg></span>
								<span class="elementor-toggle-icon-opened"><svg class="elementor-toggle-icon-opened e-font-icon-svg e-fas-caret-up" viewBox="0 0 320 512" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><path d="M288.662 352H31.338c-17.818 0-26.741-21.543-14.142-34.142l128.662-128.662c7.81-7.81 20.474-7.81 28.284 0l128.662 128.662c12.6 12.599 3.676 34.142-14.142 34.142z"></path></svg></span>
													</span>
												<a class="elementor-toggle-title" tabindex="0">Cloud Repatriation</a>
					</div>

					<div id="elementor-tab-content-1575" class="elementor-tab-content elementor-clearfix" data-tab="5" role="region" aria-labelledby="elementor-tab-title-1575"><p><span style="font-weight: 400;">The process of moving applications or workloads from a cloud environment back to internally controlled infrastructure.</span></p></div>
				</div>
							<div class="elementor-toggle-item">
					<div id="elementor-tab-title-1576" class="elementor-tab-title" data-tab="6" role="button" aria-controls="elementor-tab-content-1576" aria-expanded="false">
												<span class="elementor-toggle-icon elementor-toggle-icon-left" aria-hidden="true">
															<span class="elementor-toggle-icon-closed"><svg class="e-font-icon-svg e-fas-caret-right" viewBox="0 0 192 512" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><path d="M0 384.662V127.338c0-17.818 21.543-26.741 34.142-14.142l128.662 128.662c7.81 7.81 7.81 20.474 0 28.284L34.142 398.804C21.543 411.404 0 402.48 0 384.662z"></path></svg></span>
								<span class="elementor-toggle-icon-opened"><svg class="elementor-toggle-icon-opened e-font-icon-svg e-fas-caret-up" viewBox="0 0 320 512" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><path d="M288.662 352H31.338c-17.818 0-26.741-21.543-14.142-34.142l128.662-128.662c7.81-7.81 20.474-7.81 28.284 0l128.662 128.662c12.6 12.599 3.676 34.142-14.142 34.142z"></path></svg></span>
													</span>
												<a class="elementor-toggle-title" tabindex="0">Transition Assistance</a>
					</div>

					<div id="elementor-tab-content-1576" class="elementor-tab-content elementor-clearfix" data-tab="6" role="region" aria-labelledby="elementor-tab-title-1576"><p><span style="font-weight: 400;">A vendor&#8217;s contractual obligation to support a customer&#8217;s migration away from its platform for a defined period, typically 90 to 180 days.</span></p></div>
				</div>
								</div>
						</div>
					</div>
		</div>
					</div>
		</section>
